    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0537" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg533"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/14951</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Department of State to the Chinese Embassy
                        </hi><anchor n="5" xml:id="d511-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1939-05-01">undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The Chinese Embassy’s <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> of April 14
                    relating to proposed principles of cooperation in the Far East has been read
                    with care.</p>
                <pb facs="0538" n="534" xml:id="pg534"/>
                <p>It is believed that the Chinese Embassy is fully aware of this Government’s
                    attitude on the subject of cooperation and parallel action. Clear indications of
                    this attitude are given in the texts of documents which have been released to
                    the press by the Department of State and by the White House.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d511-f1" n="5" type="source" xml:id="d511-f1-content">
                <p>Read as an oral statement and handed to the Chinese Ambassador on May 1 by the
                    Adviser on Political Relations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
